# hookbox fixtures and goldens are byte-exact test inputs.
#
# The host has core.autocrlf enabled. Without this file, Git would normalize
# request bodies and expected event files on checkout, changing the very bytes
# the contract tests compare (events end in a single LF, stdout in CRLF).
# `whitespace=cr-at-eol` keeps `git diff --check` from treating the intentional
# CRLF bytes in stdout.txt/help.txt as trailing whitespace.
* -text whitespace=cr-at-eol
